      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "There is a complex anatomic and physiologic relationship among head and neck structures. Because of this complexity, patients with problems in any of these structures often present with a wide range of symptoms and physical findings. The authors describe many head and neck conditions that are encountered in a busy practice and emphasize selection of diagnostic studies and appropriate referral for treatment."},
